title: Microsoft Hyper-V Cluster: Network state
agents: windows
catalog: os/networking
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors the state of the networks of a Microsoft Windows failover
 cluster running Hyper-V.

 The check is {OK} if the network is up, {WARN} if it is partitioned,
 {CRIT} if it is down or unavailable and {UNKNOWN} for any other state.

 The data is collected by the agent plug-in {hyperv_cluster.ps1}, which can be
 deployed with the agent bakery rule "Hyper-V".

item:
 The name of the cluster network.

discovery:
 One service is created for each cluster network.

cluster:
 Every node of the failover cluster reports all cluster networks, so without a
 Checkmk cluster host the services are created on every node. In a Checkmk
 cluster host the report of the first node, in the order of the node names,
 is used.
